WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
China's AI pop star is pregnant. Has it all gone too far?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.160
China's AI boom is blurring the line between fiction and reality,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.380
even for digitally savvy young fans.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.040
When AI-generated girl band Baby Queen announced that singer Mitty was leaving

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.800
because she was pregnant, followers were baffled.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.160
They knew the band wasn't real.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.720
One of the saner comments asked,

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.180
could she claim maternity pay?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.260
While Western audiences often distrust AI-generated characters,

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.980
Chinese users have embraced them,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.280
encouraged by authorities backing China's race for technological leadership.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.320
This is now becoming a major industry. The first full-length AI-generated feature film opened on

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.400
Friday, but short-form dramas are really driving the boom. Reportedly, 90% of social media video

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.940
dramas are now AI-generated. Their fictional stars are becoming lucrative influencers.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.860
Fang Tao Zhe, the AI heroine of Laid Off Girl, attracted millions of fans and can charge around

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.540
£25,000 for a one-minute advert. But her promotion of contact lenses raised an obvious question.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.300
How could someone with no eyes vouch for their comfort?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.600
The advert was removed amid accusations of false representation.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.000
Other creations have caused more troubling confusion.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.680
Xiao Hai, or Good Kid, is an AI teenager whose hard luck stories persuade viewers,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.800
particularly older women, to buy products.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.640
Some apparently believed he was real.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.980
Police reported elderly women trying to travel to his hometown to help him.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.000
Online users retaliated with parodies depicting Xiao Hai as a scammer or criminal.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.400
Chinese authorities have restricted AI companions and unauthorized use of real people's likenesses.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.780
But policing this profitable industry is proving harder.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.660
Meanwhile, Baby Queen's supposedly pregnant singer

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.040
could have found a new commercial opportunity,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.920
becoming a baby and maternity product influencer.
